gement conditions and i'm gonna feed  it to bees and see how it affects their  uh larval development  and then um from the growers perspective  of course  the big question is how does this affect  yield we did see more visits to squash  plants grown in  uh organic soils as well as in soils  with plants with less powdery mildew  so  the implication of that could be that  yield is higher but it also might not be  so that's something else i'd like to  look at in the future  um  yeah um and i think that's that's all i  wanted to talk about today so i just  wanted to thank everyone in my lab and  at cornell farm services who  helped me with this project as well as  all the funders and i'd be delighted to  take questions or  hear some discussion of this work  thank you so much julie are there any  questions  i don't see any so julie i do want to  thank you and all the speakers for a uh  really fascinating session a little  different than what we've  what we typically  have at the expo and uh really some  things that make us think and lots of  additional research will be coming down  the road i think from this work so again  thank you to  everyone  um  this has been a production of cornell  university on the web at cornell.edu  this has been a production of cornell  university on the web at cornell.edu


